md) §E.3. The compiler emits no private\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:480:Artifact policy is also shared with LLVM: `docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:997–1011,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:189:> `debruijn-linearize`, `debruijn-register-compile`, removed at 8e). The\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1249:- [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](./yin.vm.rust-kernel.md): shared Rust crates, `Value` ownership, transition reuse, and LLVM sibling relationship.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1259:only dao.stream adapters (§E.3) cross into the composition. The single-port rule\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1372:[yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1428:(`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1185–1199`). The guest-agnostic differential\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1446:- tail-site fixtures for every row of the Rust design's §7.3 call-outcome table (including a tail primitive value and a tail primitive effect returning into a caller in another body, and halting with `K` empty; `docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:833–918`),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1681:(`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1201–1228`):\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:363:now operate inside wasm; §E.3 replaces the dissolved protocol; §E.4 hosts only\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:370:[yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](./yin.vm.rust-kernel.md), [yin.vm.linker.md](./yin.vm.linker.md).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:433:explicitly not NaN-boxed (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:324–392, 1238–1244`).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:439:materializing constants per task (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:394–432, 553–563`).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:507:`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1136–1145`, extended for the current\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:549:Owner decomposition, 2026-10-19: the former §E.3 content moved there unchanged;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:557:Node/browser, Wasmtime and Wasmer provide the same stream implementation (§E.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:577:(`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1134–1158`), compiled to\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:584:compiled wasm bodies and future LLVM helpers (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:991–995, 1308–1311`).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:589:mandatory (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:639–713`). Panics are kernel defects,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:593:(lines 1154–1158).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:596:DEFERRED wasm artifact item (lines 1294–1300), not the K3 review gate for K4 or\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:600:R is executable checksum despite older Rust topology wording (lines 282–318,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:701:artifact-cache policy (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:997–1011, 1113–1122,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:721:[`yin.vm.rust-kernel.md`](./yin.vm.rust-kernel.md), this specification\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:725:second kit (`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1185–1199`, equivalence law at\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:866:(`docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1167–1182, 1215–1228`). Full register slice\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:891:original lines 1–1334. Adapter names in §E.3.1 are proposed imports for this implementation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nD=Path('docs/design')\n# All old Rust document references occur in these three companion specs.\nnum={\n'324–392, 1238–1244':'§4.1 and §11 K-D2',\n'394–432, 553–563':'§4.2 and §4.6',\n'1136–1145':'§9', '1134–1158':'§9',\n'991–995, 1308–1311':'§7.4 and §12 risk 2',\n'639–713':'§§5.3–5.5',\n'997–1011, 1113–1122, 1261–1263':'§7.5, §8.4 and §11 K-D7',\n'1185–1199':'§10 K0', '1167–1182, 1215–1228':'§10',\n'1294–1300':'§11 Deferred', '805–831':'§7.2', '833–918':'§7.3',\n'1201–1228':'§10 K1–K5'}\nfor n in ['yin.vm.engine','yang.wasm','yin.vm.debruijn.register']:\n p=D/(n+'.md');s=p.read_text()\n def cite(m):\n  k=' '.join(m.group(1).split())\n  assert k in num,k\n  return '\"'`yin.vm.rust-engine.md` '\"'+num[k]\n s=re.sub(r'\"'`docs/design/yin'\"\\\\.vm\\\\.rust-kernel\\\\.md:([0-9–,\\\\s]+)\"'`'\"',cite,s)\n s=s.replace('yin.vm.rust-kernel.md','yin.vm.rust-engine.md')\n s=s.replace('[yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3','[dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md) §§1–3')\n s=s.replace('implementation specified in engine §E.3','implementation specified in dao.stream.wasm.md')\n s=s.replace('only dao.stream adapters (§E.3)','only dao.stream adapters ([dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md))')\n s=s.replace('wasm implementation of dao.stream, and K0/W0','reference to the wasm stream implementation, and K0/W0')\n s=s.replace('the same stream implementation (§E.3)','the same stream implementation ([dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md))')\n s=s.replace('equivalence law at\\\\n\"'`:805–831`'\"','equivalence law at §7.2')\n s=s.replace('Rust-design references preserve the\\\\noriginal lines 1–1334. Adapter names in §E.3.1 are proposed imports for this implementation.', 'Rust-design references use sections of [yin.vm.rust-engine.md](./yin.vm.rust-engine.md).\\\\nAdapter names in [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md) §1 are proposed imports.')\n s=s.replace('Rust-design line references\\\\nretain r5\\\\'s coordinates; the related-spec additions to that document do not shift its existing\\\\nlines.', 'Rust-design references now use sections of yin.vm.rust-engine.md under the\\\\n2026-10-19 owner decomposition; the old line-coordinate constraint is lifted.')\n p.write_text(s)\n# remaining context-dependent Rust ranges\np=D/'yin.vm.engine.md';s=p.read_text()\nfor a,b in [('(lines 1154–1158)','(Rust engine §9)'),('(lines 1294–1300)','(Rust engine §11 Deferred)'),('(lines 282–318,\\\\n997–1011)','(Rust engine §§3, 7.5)'),('(434–448, 1245–1246)','(Rust engine §4.2 and §11 K-D2b)'),('(677–678)','(Rust engine §5.3)'),('(93–95, 1164–1165)','(Rust engine §§1, 10)'),('including Level-2 engine work','including shared engine work')]:s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('now operate inside wasm; §E.3 replaces the dissolved protocol; §E.4 hosts only','now operate inside wasm; §E.3 points to the extracted implementation; §E.4 hosts only')\np.write_text(s)\np=D/'yang.wasm.md';s=p.read_text()\na=s.index('implementation specified in [dao.stream.wasm.md]');b=s.index('The 2026-10-19 decomposition remains:',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''implementation specified in [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md) §§1–3.\nThe historical service-protocol and taxonomy rulings have one home in\n[datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) §§2–5. Engine-in-guest is mandatory,\nnot a W6 experiment. Owner decomposition, 2026-10-19: this compiler plan now\nreferences the extracted doctrine and stream implementation specs.\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('engine representation/implementation/conformance\\\\nmethod live in [\"'`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E'\"','engine representation/conformance\\\\nmethod live in [\"'`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E'\"')\n# actual text uses non-backtick links\ns=s.replace('engine representation/implementation/conformance\\\\nmethod live in [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E','engine representation/conformance\\\\nmethod live in [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E')\ns=s.replace('revision 2 is an authority for\\\\nthe native implementation: status and subordination at lines 3–35, crates at 1134–1158,\\\\ndecisions at 1234–1265. It remains **design-only, not authorized for implementation**.', 'retains the revision 2 technical core and is an authority for\\\\nthe shared implementation: opening status/authorities, crate workspace (§9)\\\\nand decisions (§11). It remains **design-only**; the wasm plan depends on its\\\\nshared crates without commissioning unrelated K4/full-K5 work.')\nfor a,b in [('(§3, lines 282–318; §7.5, lines 997–1011)','(§§3, 7.5)'),('(lines 434–448, 1245–1246)','(§4.2 and §11 K-D2b)'),('(lines 93–95, 1164–1165)','(§§1, 10)'),('(lines 677–678)','(§5.3)'),('(§6.3, lines 748–781; §10, lines 1170–1182)','(§§6.3, 10)'),('Owner question 1 (lines 1282–1284) and C1/A3 (lines 243–258, 1275–1277)','Owner resolution 1 (§11) and C1/A3 (§2.7 and §11)'),('at 1285–1292','in §11'),('(§7.3, lines 833–918)','(§7.3)'),('needs Level-2 engine services','needs shared engine services'),('a Level-1 offload service','the superseded offload role')]:s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('This plan explicitly **supersedes only the DEFERRED item “WASM as an artifact target”**','This plan **supersedes the DEFERRED item “WASM as an artifact target”**')\ns=s.replace('Its other deferred items and K3-owner-review','The Rust engine rescope also adds the host adapters (§6.4); unrelated deferred items and K3-owner-review')\np.write_text(s)\np=D/'yin.vm.debruijn.register.md';s=p.read_text();a=s.index('> Owner boundary clarification, 2026-10-19');b=s.index(\\\"> Wasmer's full-suite gate\\\",a)\ns=s[:a]+'''> Owner boundary clarification and decomposition, 2026-10-19: the Rust engine\n> executes inside wasm; eight-field synchronization is internal. Doctrine and\n> historical supersessions live in [datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md);\n> the adapter implementation lives in [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md).\n> Fixtures and register transition semantics survive unchanged.\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('engine method/implementation live in\\\\n> engine §E','engine method lives in\\\\n> engine §E; the stream implementation lives in dao.stream.wasm.md')\np.write_text(s)\nprint('repointed all Rust citations and adapter references; centralized doctrine notes')\nPY\nrg -n 'rust-kernel|lines [0-9]|at [0-9]{3,}|§E\\\\.3\\\\.[123]|1–1334|Level-[012]' docs/design/{datom.world.abi,dao.stream.wasm,yin.vm.engine,yin.vm.debruijn.register,yang.wasm,yin.vm.rust-engine}.md\nrg -l 'yin.vm.rust-kernel' docs --glob '*.md'\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
