entation lives in [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md).\n> Fixtures and register transition semantics survive unchanged.\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('engine method/implementation live in\\\\n> engine §E','engine method lives in\\\\n> engine §E; the stream implementation lives in dao.stream.wasm.md')\np.write_text(s)\nprint('repointed all Rust citations and adapter references; centralized doctrine notes')\nPY\nrg -n 'rust-kernel|lines [0-9]|at [0-9]{3,}|§E\\\\.3\\\\.[123]|1–1334|Level-[012]' docs/design/{datom.world.abi,dao.stream.wasm,yin.vm.engine,yin.vm.debruijn.register,yang.wasm,yin.vm.rust-engine}.md\nrg -l 'yin.vm.rust-kernel' docs --glob '*.md'\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"repointed all Rust citations and adapter references; centralized doctrine notes\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust-engine.md:25:**Owner supersession, 2026-10-19:** the Level-1 remote-step/offload role and its\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust-engine.md:705:the former Level-1 architecture is superseded by the 2026-10-19 ruling.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:860:W2=K2 restore plus park subset; W3–W4=required Level-2 engine library coverage;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:876:Level-2 crates are substantial required work. Preserve persistent snapshots over\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1681:- **K5:** Level-2 engine parity and blocked-machine wire round-trips with JVM R4 in both directions.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
