{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Created:\n\n- [datom.world.abi.md](docs/design/datom.world.abi.md): seven sections—system ABI; taxonomy; custody; owner rulings; naming/floor; effects/events; adapter discipline.\n- [dao.stream.wasm.md](docs/design/dao.stream.wasm.md): three sections—import surface; outcomes/buffers; canonical bytes/authority.\n\nRenamed and rescoped:\n\n- `yin.vm.rust-kernel.md` → [yin.vm.rust-engine.md](docs/design/yin.vm.rust-engine.md). Retains sections 1–12: scope, invariants, topology, memory, execution, effects, LLVM, native peer, crates, phases, decisions, risks. New §6.4 owns the Rust host-adapter implementation plan.\n\nModified:\n\n- [datom.world.md](docs/design/datom.world.md): Host Boundaries is now two lines plus its doctrine link.\n- [dao.stream.md](docs/design/dao.stream.md): added the wasm implementation pointer.\n- [yin.vm.engine.md](docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md): §E.3 is a pointer; retained §E.4/§E.5 numbering.\n- [yin.vm.debruijn.register.md](docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md) and [yang.wasm.md](docs/design/yang.wasm.md): updated implementation and Rust citations.\n\nAll former Rust-document citations now target `yin.vm.rust-engine.md` sections:\n\n| Old coordinates | New target |\n|---|---|\n| 3–35 | Opening status/authorities |\n| 93–95; 1164–1165 | §§1, 10 |\n| 243–258; 1275–1277 | §§2.7, 11 |\n| 282–318 | §3 |\n| 324–392; 1238–1244 | §4.1; §11 K-D2 |\n| 394–432 | §4.2 |\n| 434–448; 1245–1246 | §4.2; §11 K-D2b |\n| 553–563 | §4.6 |\n| 639–713 | §§5.3–5.5 |\n| 677–678 | §5.3 |\n| 748–781 | §6.3 |\n| 805–831 | §7.2 |\n| 833–918 | §7.3 |\n| 991–995; 1308–1311 | §7.4; §12 risk 2 |\n| 997–1011 | §7.5 |\n| 1113–1122 | §8.4 |\n| 1134–1158; 1136–1145; 1154–1158 | §9 |\n| 1167–1182; 1170–1182; 1201–1228; 1215–1228 | §10 |\n| 1185–1199 | §10 K0, pointing to engine §E.5/register §10.4 |\n| 1234–1265 | §11 |\n| 1261–1263 | §11 K-D7 |\n| 1282–1284; 1285–1292 | §11 resolutions/questions |\n| 1294–1300 | §11 Deferred |\n\nOther moves: master Host Boundaries → ABI doctrine; engine §E.3.1–E.3.3 → wasm implementation §§1–3; Rust’s K0 fixture description → the existing method/fixture homes.\n\nSingle-home checks passed: doctrine and adapter tables each have one home; no old Rust filename or retired-spec references remain in `docs/design`. All affected-file links resolve. The broader sweep found four unrelated pre-existing broken links in the telemetry and legacy UDP design documents, left unchanged.\n\nNo source, tests or collab artifacts changed. Whitespace checks pass."}}
